# AWS-0024: DynamoDB point-in-time recovery not required for a Tofu state-lock table.
# The lock table holds only ephemeral LockID entries; PITR adds cost with no recovery value here.
AVD-AWS-0024

# AWS-0025: DynamoDB CMK not required for the state-lock table in this bootstrap demo.
# No CMK exists pre-bootstrap; AWS managed key is the appropriate starting point.
AVD-AWS-0025

# AWS-0089: S3 access logging not enabled on the state bucket.
# Enabling access logging requires a *separate* destination bucket, creating a circular
# dependency at bootstrap time (the bucket is the first resource in the account).
# Log to CloudTrail instead, which captures S3 data events without this dependency.
AVD-AWS-0089

# AWS-0132: S3 SSE uses aws:kms (AWS-managed key) rather than a customer CMK.
# No CMK exists before this bootstrap stack is applied; using AWS-managed KMS is the
# correct first-apply posture. Migrate to a CMK after bootstrap completes.
AVD-AWS-0132

# AWS-0178: VPC Flow Logs not enabled. Finding originates in the upstream
# terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws module (reached via module.vpc in the eks/network
# stacks), not in this repo's own HCL. Flow logs require a per-VPC CloudWatch log
# group + IAM role + retention policy — meaningful cost on every one of the three
# demo VPCs for no security value in a throwaway showcase. Enable via the module's
# enable_flow_log inputs in a real deployment.
AVD-AWS-0178

# AWS-0038: EKS control-plane logging (controller-manager / scheduler) not enabled.
# Finding is in the upstream terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws module (via module.eks),
# not this repo's HCL. Control-plane logs to CloudWatch add per-cluster ingestion
# cost with no value in a throwaway showcase; enable via the module's
# enabled_log_types input in a real deployment.
AVD-AWS-0038

# AWS-0040 / AWS-0041: EKS public endpoint enabled / reachable from 0.0.0.0/0.
# Intentional for this showcase: the cluster endpoint is public so exec-auth
# (aws eks get-token) from CI / the kubernetes+helm providers can reach it without
# a bastion or VPN. Access is still gated by IAM (EKS access entries) + the AWS
# API, not by network alone. Restrict public_access_cidrs or go private in prod.
AVD-AWS-0040
AVD-AWS-0041

# AWS-0104: node security-group egress allows all outbound (0.0.0.0/0).
# Finding is in the upstream terraform-aws-modules/eks node_groups.tf (via
# module.eks), not this repo's HCL. Unrestricted node egress is the module default
# and is required for nodes to pull images / reach the EKS + AWS APIs; tighten with
# a custom egress ruleset in a hardened deployment.
AVD-AWS-0104
